<article class="post">
  <h1>About Prybambas</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p><strong>Prybambas is a free collection of thinking games for kids ages 5–14.</strong> Our idea is simple: look a little closer, ask "why?", and check the answer — even the answer an AI gives you.</p>

    <h2>Why we made it</h2>
    <p>Kids today get answers instantly. What they need more is the habit of asking good questions, seeing consequences and inventing their own solutions. Prybambas turns these skills into short games that work on any phone or tablet, in 15 languages, with no login and no ads.</p>

    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/what-if/"><strong>What If?</strong></a> — a cause-and-effect logic game: single question, logical chain and deduction.</li>
      <li><a href="/inventor/"><strong>Inventor Lab</strong></a> — 8 TRIZ invention tools, a 30-day observation calendar, challenges and missions.</li>
      <li><a href="/coach/"><strong>AI Coach</strong></a> — language practice that pairs with the <em>One Verb a Day</em> workbooks.</li>
      <li><a href="/book/"><strong>Books Gym</strong></a> — printed workbooks that match the games.</li>
      <li><a href="/en/ideas/"><strong>Ideas</strong></a> — questions and small experiments for the dinner table.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>Children ages 5–14, parents, homeschoolers, teachers and multilingual families.</p>

    <h2>Prybambas and Kids Skill Academy</h2>
    <p>Prybambas is the free online hub of <strong>Kids Skill Academy</strong>, which publishes the printed workbooks <em>What If?</em>, <em>Think Like an Inventor</em>, <em>One Verb a Day</em> and <em>Microscope Safari</em>. The games and the books train the same skills: online for quick practice, on paper for screen-free time.</p>

    <h2>Languages</h2>
    <p>The games are available in English, Ukrainian, Romanian, Polish, German, French, Italian, Swedish, Finnish, Danish, Spanish, Portuguese, Hebrew, Japanese and Arabic.</p>

    <p><a class="btn" href="/">Play Prybambas →</a></p>
